# Pinned SSH host key for the development VPS, when one exists.
#
# A public host key is not a secret, so it belongs in Git: pinning it here makes
# a host-key change show up as a reviewable diff instead of being silently
# accepted by ssh-keyscan on the next deploy.
#
# Record it out of band — from the VPS console, not over the network you are
# trying to authenticate:
#
#   ssh-keyscan -t ed25519 <host>          # only to compare
#   ssh-keygen -lf /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key.pub    # run ON the host
#
# Verify the fingerprints match before committing. Format:
#   [host]:port ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
